When the collector rewrite adds a root to a safepoint's call, it makes the
call again with the larger list and erases the old one. The live sets of
the blocks still to come, and the type_infos found, held the old call, and
a later safepoint read it, freed: a crash in merkc now and then, or, once
its memory held the next call made, a root that was not one. Here the
receive loop's calls, whose results are live into other blocks, are made
again; valgrind finds no read of freed memory.

REQUIRES: valgrind, amdgpu-registered-target
RUN: %valgrind merkc -fc1 -O2 -fopenmp -emit-obj %S/omp-target-receive-ring.m -o %t.o
